[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles Unified Calibration and Service Interface Test Protocol
UID: DHF-HRC-UCSI-0003-TP
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-ucsi

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This protocol defines the minimum verification tests for the Heracles Unified Calibration and Service Interface (UCSI) Software Requirements Specification, DHF-HRC-UCSI-0001.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Configuration

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless a test specifies otherwise, execute it on a fully assembled Heracles system in its approved service/test configuration. A bench test uses the machine PCBs on a bench without machine peripherals.

Manual X-ray emission testing shall be performed only by qualified personnel under the approved radiation-safety procedure and in the approved service/test configuration.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
===================  ==========================================
Abbreviation/Term    Definition
===================  ==========================================
GCB                  Gryphon Control Board
HVPS                 High Voltage Power Supply
UCSI                 Unified Calibration and Service Interface
===================  ==========================================
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TP-UCSI-
TITLE: Test Cases

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TP-UCSI-001
TITLE: UCSI deployment and telemetry monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that UCSI presents current telemetry and status information and supports numerical and graphical monitoring of selected parameters in both supported deployment modes.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Bench test setup with the GCB and HVPS telemetry channels available.

The standalone UCSI application and the system PC application containing the hosted UCSI module are installed.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the standalone UCSI application and connect the bench test setup.
2. Confirm that current operating-parameter values, communication status, system status, interlock status, and active faults are displayed.
3. Select a telemetry parameter for the monitored-parameter list and for a graph; confirm that its current numerical value and telemetry history are displayed.
4. Close the standalone application, start the system PC application, and open the hosted UCSI module.
5. Repeat steps 2 and 3.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
In both deployment modes, UCSI displays the current system operating parameters, communication status, system status, interlock status, and active faults received from the bench test setup. A selected parameter appears in the monitored-parameter list with its current value and in a graph with its telemetry history.
<<<
