[TEST_CASE]
UID: TP-UCSI-002
TITLE: Manual HVPS service control
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that UCSI commands HVPS service operating parameters and manually enables and disables X-ray emission while showing HVPS feedback and interlock status.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Fully assembled Heracles system in the approved service/test configuration.

Qualified personnel have completed the approved radiation-safety procedure for manual emission testing.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start UCSI and open the HVPS view.
2. Confirm that the HVPS feedback values and interlock indicators are displayed.
3. Command permitted HVPS operating parameters using the approved service procedure and confirm that the displayed setpoint and feedback update accordingly.
4. With the required interlocks satisfied, enable manual X-ray emission using the approved service procedure; observe the emission feedback and interlock indicators.
5. Disable manual X-ray emission and confirm that the emission feedback returns to the non-emitting state.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
UCSI displays HVPS feedback and interlock status throughout the test. Each permitted command is reflected by the displayed HVPS setpoint and feedback. UCSI enables and disables manual X-ray emission when directed by the qualified operator under the approved procedure.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-UCSI-004
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TP-UCSI-003
TITLE: Coil control and control system configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
Verify that UCSI commands coil operating parameters and views and sets control system configuration values.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
Bench test setup with the GCB and HVPS communication channels available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start UCSI and open the Coils view.
2. Confirm that the X, Y, and focus coil feedback values are displayed.
3. Command permitted values for each coil using the approved service procedure and confirm that the corresponding displayed feedback values update.
4. Open the System Config view and refresh the control system configuration values.
5. Confirm that current configuration values are displayed, set one permitted configuration value using the approved service procedure, and confirm that the displayed current value updates.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
UCSI displays the feedback value for each coil and updates the displayed feedback after each permitted coil command. UCSI displays current control system configuration values and updates the displayed current value after setting a permitted configuration value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
